<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">sit</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">sit</ansi> command sits you down to rest. <ansi fg="command">rest</ansi> does the same thing.

While sitting, your health, stamina and conviction come back
<ansi fg="white-bold">faster</ansi> than when you stand, though not as fast as when you sleep.

Sitting is safer than sleeping. You stay awake, and an attacker gets
no free critical hit on you.

<ansi fg="yellow">You get up when:</ansi>

  - You use <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi>. Getting up from a seat costs nothing.
  - You walk out of the room.
  - Someone attacks you, or you start a fight. You leap to your feet.

<ansi fg="yellow">You can't sit:</ansi>

  - In a fight.
  - While asleep, knocked down, or locked in a grapple.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help sleep</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help stand</ansi>
